{
  "description": "Declared ground-truth scenarios for estimator validation (injected, not measured). alpha_true is the assumed architecture slowdown relative to the reference arm; delta_true is the genuine implementation difference that normalisation is supposed to EXPOSE, and it is applied to evaluation workloads only. Calibration workloads carry delta = 0 by construction (both architectures run the same code there), otherwise alpha and delta are confounded.",
